        "date": "2026-11-19T22:25:04Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(kernel): machining-mesh parity for the solidcore STEP path\n\nThe solidcore STEP path (#917) needs these items below the app:\n\n- The machining mesh snaps each coordinate within 1e-9 mm of the\n  1e-3 mm grid onto that grid before the weld. A coordinate outside\n  the window never moves. A facet that collapses is dropped, and the\n  side count refuses a mesh that the drop opens.\n- A watertight mesh with a negative volume is turned outward, with a\n  note. A zero or NaN volume is still refused.\n- The STEP reader refuses an edge or swept B-spline curve that breaks\n  at an interior knot above the degree, or that has a weight that is\n  not positive, by name, before the topology read.\n- measure_within refines adaptively (depth 12, a budget of 2^21\n  samples) and adds the 1-Lipschitz bound dmax + longest side. The\n  fillet fixture now meshes at 0.005 mm. Two Solidcraft pins change\n  (see docs/decisions/917-kernel-parity.md, \"Changed pins\").\n- Mesh keeps one facet range per closed solid (Mesh::from_solids), and\n  slice::slice_of slices known solids that share a wall line as their\n  union.\n\nRefs #917\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
